  "message": "No runtime checks ran, so nothing here is validated yet. The emulation stopped before testing because none of our Google Cloud parts (Pub/Sub, Dataflow, Firestore, Cloud Storage, BigQuery, Vertex AI) has a supported code template yet. Changing the diagram can't fix that, so I've left it as it is; the fix is product engineering work, and the first piece would be a native Pub/Sub and Dataflow template that runs the \"unknown device gets rejected\" case end to end. While that's built, let's settle the decision that is ours to make: how long after an event's own timestamp should we still accept it, for example 10 minutes, and should anything later be rejected, stored separately or rescored?",
